Keep /data/data when wiping Data, and back it up only once

Android 15+ vold bind-mounts /data/data (user 0's CE storage, with its
fscrypt policy) onto /data/user/0. Restore first wipes Data without media,
and the recursive wipe removed /data/data while it was still mounted: the
mount then pointed at a deleted directory, /data/user/0 could not be
written, and every Data restore stopped at the first app with
"extractTarFork() process ended with ERROR: 255" (found on the owner's
rothko, 30 Oct 2026). Empty /data/data but keep the directory.

The same bind mount made backups store all app data twice (/data/data and
/data/user/0). Exclude /data/data; /data/user/0 holds the same files.

Both changes follow OrangeFox's OF_WORKAROUND_BACKUP_BUG (fox_14.1/16.0).

diff --git a/partition.cpp b/partition.cpp
index ef45ea3..7394195 100755
--- a/partition.cpp
+++ b/partition.cpp
@@ -1296,6 +1296,9 @@ void TWPartition::Setup_Data_Media() {
 		backup_exclusions.add_absolute_dir("/data/adb/ksu/modules.img"); //After ksu 0.8.x the modules.img file became 1tb, which is inhibiting the execution of backups
 		wipe_exclusions.add_absolute_dir(Mount_Point + "/misc/vold"); // adopted storage keys
 		ExcludeAll(Mount_Point + "/system/storage.xml");
+		// Android 15+: vold bind-mounts /data/data onto /data/user/0, so the same app data would be
+		// archived twice; keep the /data/user/0 copy (from OrangeFox OF_WORKAROUND_BACKUP_BUG)
+		backup_exclusions.add_absolute_dir("/data/data");
 
 		backup_exclusions.add_absolute_dir("/data/system/users/0/package-restrictions.xml");
 
@@ -2635,7 +2638,12 @@ bool TWPartition::Wipe_Data_Without_Wiping_Media_Func(const string& parent __unu
 					closedir(d);
 					return false;
 				}
-				rmdir(dir.c_str());
+				// keep /data/data itself: it is bind-mounted on /data/user/0 and holds user 0's CE
+				// policy; removing it left restore unable to write /data/user/0 (extractTarFork 255)
+				if (dir == "/data/data/")
+					LOGINFO("kept '%s' (emptied)\n", dir.c_str());
+				else
+					rmdir(dir.c_str());
